==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|de|Centromer}}, corresponding to {{affix|en|centro-|-mere}} (from {{der|en|grc|μέρος||part}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˈsɛntɹə(ʊ)mɪə/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˈsɛntɹəˌmiɚ/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|genetics}} The central region of a [[eukaryotic]] [[chromosome]] where the [[kinetochore]] is assembled.
#* {{quote-journal|en|work=Cytologia|author=C. D. Darlington|year=1936|volume=7|issue=1-2|page=242|passage=The aberrant bivalents with single terminal chiasmata are specially liable to this failure of orientation, presumably because their '''centromeres''' lie exceptionally far apart, as is the case in similar circumstances in a ''Lilium'' hybrid with reduced chiasma-frequency.|title=The Analysis of Chromosome Movements, I. ''Podophyllum versipelle''}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1999|author=w:Matt Ridley|title=Genome|publisher=Harper Perennial|year_published=2000|page=16|passage=Every chromosome has a long arm and a short arm separated by a pinch point known as a '''centromere'''.}}

